.DS_Store
node_modules
/build
/.svelte-kit
/package

# Cargo build output. Now at the workspace root rather than under src-tauri/,
# because a workspace shares one target directory across all members.
/target
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# Python bytecode, from scripts/ (the dash ratchet and its tests)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The OCR model files, their verified upstream downloads, and the generated
# NOTICE. NOTHING IS CONVERTED ANY MORE: scripts/acquire-ppocr-detector.py and
# scripts/acquire-ppocr-recogniser.py both DOWNLOAD Baidu's own ONNX and verify
# it (ADR-0036 for the detector, ADR-0037 for the recogniser), and
# scripts/write-model-notice.py generates the NOTICE from the pins.
#
# ⚠️ This named scripts/convert-ppocr-models.py as converting "the recogniser
# and the dictionary" until 2026-09-06. That script is DELETED -- ADR-0037 took
# the recogniser to Baidu's ONNX too, so it converted nothing UP-TAKE ships.
# The paragraph directly below still describes correcting this same block's
# provenance claim at PR #88 round 10; this is the third time this block has
# been wrong about which scripts exist, and the second time it was wrong about
# the word "converts".
#
# NEVER committed. ADR-0034's conversion route is superseded by ADR-0036 and
# ADR-0037, and ADR-0003 sets the licence this repository ships under,
# GPL-3.0-or-later with a CLA: ~31 MB of third-party
# model weights do not belong in its history, where they would be permanent.
# The manifest in crates/uptake-assets/src/ppocr.rs carries their digests, which
# is the part that IS ours to version.
/dist

# The staging directory the installer packages: the ONNX Runtime DLL, its two
# notice files, and the OCR models. ~47.6 MB of binaries that are ACQUIRED
# rather than committed -- `scripts/acquire-onnxruntime.py`,
# `scripts/acquire-ppocr-detector.py` and `scripts/acquire-ppocr-recogniser.py`
# each verify every byte against a pinned SHA-256 before writing here, which is
# ADR-0032 decision 2. The exact figure is 47,608,523 B, and
# `installer_payload_bytes()` derives it from the six pins -- do not hand-write
# a total here, which is how the "~31 MB" below went stale in the first place.
#
# ⚠️ This block said "the converted PP-OCRv4 models", named TWO scripts, and
# said ~31 MB. All three were stale, and it sits eleven lines below the block
# this pull request edited specifically to correct the same provenance claim --
# PR #88 round 10, FINDING 2. The detector is Baidu's own ONNX and is not
# converted here (ADR-0036). Committing them
# would put unreviewable binaries in a public repository and make the pin a
# description rather than a check.
/src-tauri/assets
